IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `P5-section-5`

-- P5-art-44-45-46: Article 44 (certificates), Article 45 (information obligations of notified bodies) and Article 46 (derogation from the
-- conformity assessment procedure). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026 (a plain-text
-- rendering with no legal effect; src:N is its line N). Group: General (Art 113 second paragraph, assumed: keel fork F-113-groups).
-- The Omnibus changed none of these three Articles (no marker in lines 695 to 722), so there is one text and no dispatcher on the version.
-- A notified body, a market surveillance authority, the Commission and a Member State are not operators (Art 3(8)): their provisions pass the
-- date only. A law-enforcement or civil protection authority that puts a system into service is a deployer: Article 46(2) and (7) pass the
-- route, placement date and design change of the system, and Art 111(2) may save it.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text's own yes / no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md).

§ `Article 44: certificates`

DECLARE `Art 44 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 44(1) draw up the certificate in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities`
    `Art 44(2) extend the validity of a certificate`
    `Art 44(3) suspend or withdraw the certificate or impose restrictions on it`
    `Art 44(3) give reasons for the decision`

§§ `Article 44(1): the language of the certificate`

-- src:697 | 1. Certificates issued by notified bodies in accordance with Annex VII shall be drawn-up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities in the Member State in which the notified body is established.
@ref Art 44(1) (src:697)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the certificate is issued by a notified body in accordance with Annex VII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 44(1) the certificate must be drawn up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities of the Member State in which the notified body is established` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the certificate is issued by a notified body in accordance with Annex VII`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Certificates issued by notified bodies in accordance with Annex VII" (a scope limit with no "only")

§§ `Article 44(2): the period of validity, its extension, and supplements`

-- First sentence: the period the certificate indicates "shall not exceed five years for AI systems covered by Annex I, and four years for AI systems covered by Annex III".
-- A system covered by both Annexes (Article 43(3) fourth subparagraph) has both limits, so the shorter binds: fork F-44-2-both (NOTES.md).
-- src:698 | 2. Certificates shall be valid for the period they indicate, which shall not exceed five years for AI systems covered by Annex I, and four years for AI systems covered by Annex III.
@ref Art 44(2) first sentence (src:698)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is covered by Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is covered by Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the AI system is covered by Annex III`
         THEN JUST 4  -- fork F-44-2-both: where the system is covered by both Annexes, the shorter limit
         ELSE IF `the AI system is covered by Annex I`
              THEN JUST 5
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names AI systems covered by Annex I and by Annex III only

-- The period the certificate indicates is computed from the two dates the certificate states, its first and its last day of validity (fork F-44-2-period): it does not exceed the limit
-- where the last day is at most the day before the anniversary of the first day that falls the limit's number of years later. A caller no longer rounds the period to whole years.
-- src:698 | 2. Certificates shall be valid for the period they indicate, which shall not exceed five years for AI systems covered by Annex I, and four years for AI systems covered by Annex III.
@ref Art 44(2) first sentence: is the indicated period within the limit (src:698)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is covered by Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is covered by Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of validity the certificate indicates` IS A DATE
      `the last day of validity the certificate indicates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` `the date asked` `the AI system is covered by Annex I` `the AI system is covered by Annex III`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no limit on these facts
    WHEN JUST `the limit` THEN JUST (`the last day of validity the certificate indicates` AT MOST ((Date (DATE_DAY `the first day of validity the certificate indicates`) (DATE_MONTH `the first day of validity the certificate indicates`) ((DATE_YEAR `the first day of validity the certificate indicates`) PLUS `the limit`)) MINUS 1))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not exceed"; the last day is the day before the anniversary (fork F-44-2-period)

-- Second sentence, first limb: "At the request of the provider, the validity of a certificate may be extended for further periods ... based on a re-assessment".
-- Two gates on one "may", both answered NOTHING when they fail: "At the request of the provider" is not "where", "when" or "upon" (the gate words on a "may" that the Guide's rulings of 2026-11-05 turn into JUST FALSE),
-- so the ruling of 2026-11-12 (BRIEF.md: a function named for a grant answers NOTHING when an "if" gate fails) and the Guide's "Everywhere else it answers NOTHING" give NOTHING; "based on a re-assessment" is a basis
-- that the text does not close with "only": no re-assessment gives NOTHING (the grant rule). Fork F-44-2-extension; split site (ii).
-- src:698 | At the request of the provider, the validity of a certificate may be extended for further periods, each not exceeding five years for AI systems covered by Annex I, and four years for AI systems covered by Annex III, based on a re-assessment in accordance with the applicable conformity assessment procedures.
@ref Art 44(2) second sentence (src:698)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the provider has requested the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the validity is extended based on a re-assessment in accordance with the applicable conformity assessment procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF NOT `the provider has requested the extension`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the request of the provider" (a gate on a "may" that is not "where", "when" or "upon": the ruling of 2026-11-12 in BRIEF.md; fork F-44-2-extension)
         ELSE IF `the validity is extended based on a re-assessment in accordance with the applicable conformity assessment procedures`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "based on a re-assessment" (a grant: fork F-44-2-extension)

-- Third sentence: "Any supplement to a certificate shall remain valid, provided that the certificate which it supplements is valid." A "provided that" on a statement of status, not
-- on a "may": where the certificate is not valid the supplement does not remain valid (the text's own no, "if" variant): fork F-44-2-supplement.
-- src:698 | Any supplement to a certificate shall remain valid, provided that the certificate which it supplements is valid.
@ref Art 44(2) last sentence (src:698)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the certificate which the supplement supplements is valid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 44(2) the supplement to a certificate remains valid` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the certificate which the supplement supplements is valid`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that the certificate which it supplements is valid" (fork F-44-2-supplement)

§§ `Article 44(3): suspension, withdrawal and restriction, reasons, and appeal`

-- First sentence. "Where a notified body finds ..." is a "where" gate on a duty: no such finding gives JUST FALSE (the periods ruling (b)); "unless compliance ... is ensured by
-- appropriate corrective action taken by the provider ... within an appropriate deadline set by the notified body": once met, JUST FALSE (the text's own "unless"; decided case by case, fork F-44-3-unless).
-- "taking account of the principle of proportionality" is a manner of acting and is not a gate: which of the three measures is left to the notified body (the act is "suspend or withdraw ... or impose restrictions").
-- src:699 | 3. Where a notified body finds that an AI system no longer meets the requirements set out in Section 2, it shall, taking account of the principle of proportionality, suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it, unless compliance with those requirements is ensured by appropriate corrective action taken by the provider of the system within an appropriate deadline set by the notified body.
@ref Art 44(3) first sentence (src:699)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body finds that the AI system no longer meets the requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compliance with those requirements is ensured by appropriate corrective action taken by the provider within an appropriate deadline set by the notified body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF NOT `the notified body finds that the AI system no longer meets the requirements set out in Section 2`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a notified body finds that an AI system no longer meets the requirements" (a "where" gate on a duty: reading (b))
         ELSE IF `compliance with those requirements is ensured by appropriate corrective action taken by the provider within an appropriate deadline set by the notified body`
              THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless compliance ... is ensured by appropriate corrective action" (fork F-44-3-unless)
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:699 | The notified body shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Art 44(3) second sentence (src:699)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has taken a decision under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 44(3) the notified body must give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `the notified body has taken a decision under this paragraph`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "its decision" (there is no decision to give reasons for)

-- Last sentence: "An appeal procedure against decisions of the notified bodies, including on conformity certificates issued, shall be available." The text does not say who provides it:
-- an existence function and no rule (no bearer to put in a PARTY clause; NOTES.md, Jural relations).
-- src:700 | An appeal procedure against decisions of the notified bodies, including on conformity certificates issued, shall be available.
@ref Art 44(3) last paragraph (src:700)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 44(3) an appeal procedure against decisions of the notified bodies must be available` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Article 44: the regulative rules`

@ref Art 44(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the certificate is issued by a notified body in accordance with Annex VII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 44 act`
`Art 44(1) the notified body's duty to draw up the certificate in a language which can be easily understood` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 44(1) the certificate must be drawn up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities of the Member State in which the notified body is established` `the date asked` `the certificate is issued by a notified body in accordance with Annex VII`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MUST `Art 44(1) draw up the certificate in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 44(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the provider has requested the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the validity is extended based on a re-assessment in accordance with the applicable conformity assessment procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 44 act`
`Art 44(2) the notified body's permission to extend the validity of a certificate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` `the date asked` `the provider has requested the extension` `the validity is extended based on a re-assessment in accordance with the applicable conformity assessment procedures`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MAY `Art 44(2) extend the validity of a certificate`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is permitted here on these facts

@ref Art 44(3) first sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body finds that the AI system no longer meets the requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compliance with those requirements is ensured by appropriate corrective action taken by the provider within an appropriate deadline set by the notified body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 44 act`
`Art 44(3) the notified body's duty to suspend or withdraw the certificate or impose restrictions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` `the date asked` `the notified body finds that the AI system no longer meets the requirements set out in Section 2` `compliance with those requirements is ensured by appropriate corrective action taken by the provider within an appropriate deadline set by the notified body`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MUST `Art 44(3) suspend or withdraw the certificate or impose restrictions on it`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 44(3) second sentence
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has taken a decision under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 44 act`
`Art 44(3) the notified body's duty to give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 44(3) the notified body must give reasons for its decision` `the date asked` `the notified body has taken a decision under this paragraph`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MUST `Art 44(3) give reasons for the decision`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 45: information obligations of notified bodies`

DECLARE `Art 45 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 45(1) inform the notifying authority`
    `Art 45(2) inform the other notified bodies`
    `Art 45(3) provide the other notified bodies with relevant information`
    `Art 45(4) safeguard the confidentiality of the information obtained`

§§ `Article 45(1): information to the notifying authority`

DECLARE `Art 45(1) item` IS ONE OF
    `Art 45(1)(a) certificates, supplements and quality management system approvals issued`
    `Art 45(1)(b) refusal, restriction, suspension or withdrawal of a certificate or approval`
    `Art 45(1)(c) circumstances affecting the scope of or conditions for notification`
    `Art 45(1)(d) a request for information from a market surveillance authority`
    `Art 45(1)(e) conformity assessment activities performed and any other activity, on request`

-- Items (a) to (d): the duty is to inform of "any" such event; where the event has not occurred there is nothing to inform of, and the paragraph does not say there is no duty (NOTHING,
-- a scope limit with no "only"). Item (e) is "on request": no request gives JUST FALSE (the periods ruling (b), rule (c)); fork F-45-1-e.
-- src:703 | 1. Notified bodies shall inform the notifying authority of the following:
-- src:704 | (a) any Union technical documentation assessment certificates, any supplements to those certificates, and any quality management system approvals issued in accordance with the requirements of Annex VII;
-- src:705 | (b) any refusal, restriction, suspension or withdrawal of a Union technical documentation assessment certificate or a quality management system approval issued in accordance with the requirements of Annex VII;
-- src:706 | (c) any circumstances affecting the scope of or conditions for notification;
-- src:707 | (d) any request for information which they have received from market surveillance authorities regarding conformity assessment activities;
-- src:708 | (e) on request, conformity assessment activities performed within the scope of their notification and any other activity performed, including cross-border activities and subcontracting.
@ref Art 45(1) (src:703-708)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the item of information` IS A `Art 45(1) item`
      `the event the item describes has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 45(1) the notified body must inform the notifying authority of the item` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE CONSIDER `the item of information`
         WHEN `Art 45(1)(e) conformity assessment activities performed and any other activity, on request` THEN
             IF `the notifying authority has requested the information`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on request" (a gate on a duty: fork F-45-1-e)
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the event the item describes has occurred`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any ... issued" / "any refusal" / "any circumstances" / "any request": nothing of that kind has occurred

§§ `Article 45(2): information to the other notified bodies`

DECLARE `Art 45(2) item` IS ONE OF
    `Art 45(2)(a) quality management system approvals refused, suspended or withdrawn`
    `Art 45(2)(a) quality system approvals issued, on request`
    `Art 45(2)(b) certificates or supplements refused, withdrawn, suspended or otherwise restricted`
    `Art 45(2)(b) certificates and supplements issued, on request`

-- src:709 | 2. Each notified body shall inform the other notified bodies of:
-- src:710 | (a) quality management system approvals which it has refused, suspended or withdrawn, and, upon request, of quality system approvals which it has issued;
-- src:711 | (b) Union technical documentation assessment certificates or any supplements thereto which it has refused, withdrawn, suspended or otherwise restricted, and, upon request, of the certificates and/or supplements thereto which it has issued.
@ref Art 45(2) (src:709-711)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the item of information to the other notified bodies` IS A `Art 45(2) item`
      `the event the item describes has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another notified body has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 45(2) the notified body must inform the other notified bodies of the item` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE CONSIDER `the item of information to the other notified bodies`
         WHEN `Art 45(2)(a) quality system approvals issued, on request` THEN
             IF `another notified body has requested the information`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon request" (a gate on a duty: fork F-45-1-e)
         WHEN `Art 45(2)(b) certificates and supplements issued, on request` THEN
             IF `another notified body has requested the information`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon request" (a gate on a duty: fork F-45-1-e)
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the event the item describes has occurred`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which it has refused, suspended or withdrawn": nothing of that kind has occurred

§§ `Article 45(3) and (4): similar notified bodies, and confidentiality`

DECLARE `Art 45(3) kind of result` IS ONE OF
    `Art 45(3) negative conformity assessment results`
    `Art 45(3) positive conformity assessment results, on request`

-- src:712 | 3. Each notified body shall provide the other notified bodies carrying out similar conformity assessment activities covering the same types of AI systems with relevant information on issues relating to negative and, on request, positive conformity assessment results.
@ref Art 45(3) (src:712)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the kind of conformity assessment results` IS A `Art 45(3) kind of result`
      `the other notified body carries out similar conformity assessment activities covering the same types of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other notified body has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 45(3) the notified body must provide the other notified body with relevant information on the kind of results` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF NOT `the other notified body carries out similar conformity assessment activities covering the same types of AI systems`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the other notified bodies carrying out similar conformity assessment activities covering the same types of AI systems" (a scope limit with no "only")
         ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of conformity assessment results`
              WHEN `Art 45(3) negative conformity assessment results` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `Art 45(3) positive conformity assessment results, on request` THEN
                  IF `the other notified body has requested the information`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on request" (a gate on a duty: fork F-45-1-e)

-- src:713 | 4. Notified bodies shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain, in accordance with Article 78.
@ref Art 45(4) (src:713)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 45(4) the notified body must safeguard the confidentiality of the information that it obtains, in accordance with Article 78` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Article 45: the regulative rules`

-- None of these states a time limit or a consequence: no breach path (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref Art 45(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the item of information` IS A `Art 45(1) item`
      `the event the item describes has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notifying authority has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 45 act`
`Art 45(1) the notified body's duty to inform the notifying authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 45(1) the notified body must inform the notifying authority of the item` `the date asked` `the item of information` `the event the item describes has occurred` `the notifying authority has requested the information`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MUST `Art 45(1) inform the notifying authority`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 45(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the item of information to the other notified bodies` IS A `Art 45(2) item`
      `the event the item describes has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another notified body has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 45 act`
`Art 45(2) the notified body's duty to inform the other notified bodies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 45(2) the notified body must inform the other notified bodies of the item` `the date asked` `the item of information to the other notified bodies` `the event the item describes has occurred` `another notified body has requested the information`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MUST `Art 45(2) inform the other notified bodies`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 45(3)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the kind of conformity assessment results` IS A `Art 45(3) kind of result`
      `the other notified body carries out similar conformity assessment activities covering the same types of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other notified body has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 45 act`
`Art 45(3) the notified body's duty to provide the other notified bodies with relevant information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 45(3) the notified body must provide the other notified body with relevant information on the kind of results` `the date asked` `the kind of conformity assessment results` `the other notified body carries out similar conformity assessment activities covering the same types of AI systems` `the other notified body has requested the information`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MUST `Art 45(3) provide the other notified bodies with relevant information`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 45(4)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 45 act`
`Art 45(4) the notified body's duty to safeguard confidentiality` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 45(4) the notified body must safeguard the confidentiality of the information that it obtains, in accordance with Article 78` `the date asked`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Notified body` MUST `Art 45(4) safeguard the confidentiality of the information obtained`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 46: derogation from the conformity assessment procedure`

DECLARE `Art 46 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 46 the market surveillance authority`
    `Art 46 the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 46 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 46(1) authorise the placing on the market or putting into service of the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 46(3) inform the Commission and the other Member States of the authorisation`
    `Art 46(5) enter into consultations with the relevant Member State`
    `Art 46(5) consult the operators concerned`
    `Art 46(5) decide whether the authorisation is justified`
    `Art 46(5) address the decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant operators`
    `Art 46(6) withdraw the authorisation`

DECLARE `Art 46 deployer act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 46(2) put the high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation`
    `Art 46(2) stop the use of the high-risk AI system with immediate effect`
    `Art 46(2) discard all the results and outputs of the use immediately`

DECLARE `Art 46(5) duty` IS ONE OF
    `Art 46(5) the Commission enters into consultations with the relevant Member State without delay`
    `Art 46(5) the operators concerned are consulted and have the possibility to present their views`
    `Art 46(5) the Commission decides whether the authorisation is justified`
    `Art 46(5) the Commission addresses its decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant operators`

§§ `Article 46(1): the authorisation`

-- "upon a duly justified request" reads like "upon" (rule (c) of 2026-11-05): no such request gives JUST FALSE. "for exceptional reasons of public security or the protection of life and health of persons,
-- environmental protection or the protection of key industrial and infrastructural assets" limits the grant in its own wording: a different reason gives NOTHING. Fork F-46-1 (split site (ii)).
-- src:716 | 1. By way of derogation from Article 43 and upon a duly justified request, any market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of specific high-risk AI systems within the territory of the Member State concerned, for exceptional reasons of public security or the protection of life and health of persons, environmental protection or the protection of key industrial and infrastructural assets.
@ref Art 46(1) first sentence (src:716)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a duly justified request has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason is an exceptional reason of public security or the protection of life and health of persons, environmental protection or the protection of key industrial and infrastructural assets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 46(1) the market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of a specific high-risk AI system within the territory of its Member State` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF NOT `a duly justified request has been made`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon a duly justified request" (a gate on a "may": reading (b), split site (ii), fork F-46-1)
         ELSE IF `the reason is an exceptional reason of public security or the protection of life and health of persons, environmental protection or the protection of key industrial and infrastructural assets`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for exceptional reasons of ..." (a limit on the grant: fork F-46-1)

