§§ `Article 46(2): urgency without the authorisation`

-- Three gates on one "may". The addressee is limited ("law-enforcement authorities or civil protection authorities"): another deployer gives NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only").
-- "In a duly justified situation of urgency ... or in the case of specific, substantial and imminent threat" is not "where", "when" or "upon": no such situation gives NOTHING (the ruling of 2026-11-12 in BRIEF.md and the Guide's "Everywhere else it answers NOTHING"; fork F-46-2).
-- "provided that such authorisation is requested during or after the use without undue delay" is a "provided that" on a grant: not requested gives NOTHING (the grant ruling). Fork F-46-2 (split site (ii)).
-- src:717 | 2. In a duly justified situation of urgency for exceptional reasons of public security or in the case of specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons, law-enforcement authorities or civil protection authorities may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation referred to in paragraph 1, provided that such authorisation is requested during or after the use without undue delay.
@ref Art 46(2) first sentence (src:717)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer is a law-enforcement authority or a civil protection authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the situation is a duly justified situation of urgency for exceptional reasons of public security, or a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation referred to in paragraph 1 is requested during or after the use without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 46 2)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF NOT `the deployer is a law-enforcement authority or a civil protection authority`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "law-enforcement authorities or civil protection authorities may" (a scope limit with no "only")
              ELSE IF NOT `the situation is a duly justified situation of urgency for exceptional reasons of public security, or a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons`
                   THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a duly justified situation of urgency ... or in the case of specific, substantial and imminent threat" (a gate on a "may" that is not "where", "when" or "upon": the ruling of 2026-11-12 in BRIEF.md; fork F-46-2)
                   ELSE IF `the authorisation referred to in paragraph 1 is requested during or after the use without undue delay`
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provided that such authorisation is requested during or after the use without undue delay" (a grant: fork F-46-2)

-- Second sentence: "If the authorisation ... is refused, the use ... shall be stopped with immediate effect and all the results and outputs of such use shall be immediately discarded."
-- An "if" on a duty: not refused gives JUST FALSE (the text's own "if"). "immediate effect" and "immediately" are promptness with no number: the rules carry no time limit (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
