§§ `Article 46(4) to (6): objection, consultation and withdrawal`

-- Paragraph 4. "Where, within 15 calendar days of receipt of the information ..., no objection has been raised by either a Member State or the Commission ..., that authorisation shall be deemed justified."
-- Objection raised: the "where" fails, JUST FALSE (reading (b)); no objection and the 15 days not yet past: not yet answerable (NOTHING); no objection and the 15 days past: JUST TRUE. A period the text fixes in its own words.
-- The days are counted from the two dates the function takes, the date asked and the date of receipt: the 15 calendar days have passed from the date of receipt plus 15 (fork F-46-4).
-- src:719 | 4. Where, within 15 calendar days of receipt of the information referred to in paragraph 3, no objection has been raised by either a Member State or the Commission in respect of an authorisation issued by a market surveillance authority of a Member State in accordance with paragraph 1, that authorisation shall be deemed justified.
@ref Art 46(4) (src:719)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date of receipt of the information referred to in paragraph 3` IS A DATE
      `an objection has been raised by a Member State within 15 calendar days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an objection has been raised by the Commission within 15 calendar days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 46(4) the authorisation is deemed justified` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF `an objection has been raised by a Member State within 15 calendar days` OR `an objection has been raised by the Commission within 15 calendar days`
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, within 15 calendar days ..., no objection has been raised" (reading (b); paragraph 5 then applies)
         ELSE IF `the date asked` AT LEAST (`the date of receipt of the information referred to in paragraph 3` PLUS 15)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 15 calendar days have not yet passed, so the authorisation is not yet deemed justified or unjustified

-- Paragraph 5, first sentence: the Commission's duty to consult arises where, within 15 calendar days, a Member State objects to an authorisation of another Member State, or the Commission considers the authorisation contrary to Union law
-- or the conclusion on compliance unfounded. The other three duties of the paragraph (the operators consulted, the decision, its address) follow from the same trigger.
-- src:720 | 5. Where, within 15 calendar days of receipt of the notification referred to in paragraph 3, objections are raised by a Member State against an authorisation issued by a market surveillance authority of another Member State, or where the Commission considers the authorisation to be contrary to Union law, or the conclusion of the Member States regarding the compliance of the system as referred to in paragraph 3 to be unfounded, the Commission shall, without delay, enter into consultations with the relevant Member State. The operators concerned shall be consulted and have the possibility to present their views. Having regard thereto, the Commission shall decide whether the authorisation is justified. The Commission shall address its decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant operators.
@ref Art 46(5) (src:720)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the duty of the paragraph` IS A `Art 46(5) duty`
      `a Member State has raised objections within 15 calendar days against an authorisation issued by the market surveillance authority of another Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers the authorisation to be contrary to Union law, or the conclusion of the Member States regarding the compliance of the system to be unfounded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 46(5) the duty of the paragraph applies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come
    ELSE IF       `a Member State has raised objections within 15 calendar days against an authorisation issued by the market surveillance authority of another Member State`
               OR `the Commission considers the authorisation to be contrary to Union law, or the conclusion of the Member States regarding the compliance of the system to be unfounded`
         THEN CONSIDER `the duty of the paragraph`
              WHEN `Art 46(5) the Commission enters into consultations with the relevant Member State without delay` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `Art 46(5) the operators concerned are consulted and have the possibility to present their views` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `Art 46(5) the Commission decides whether the authorisation is justified` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `Art 46(5) the Commission addresses its decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant operators` THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, within 15 calendar days ..., objections are raised ..., or where the Commission considers ..." (a "where" gate on a duty: reading (b))

-- src:721 | 6. Where the Commission considers the authorisation unjustified, it shall be withdrawn by the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned.
@ref Art 46(6) (src:721)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission considers the authorisation unjustified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
