      `the duty of the paragraph` IS A `Art 46(5) duty`
      `a Member State has raised objections within 15 calendar days against an authorisation issued by the market surveillance authority of another Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers the authorisation to be contrary to Union law, or the conclusion of the Member States regarding the compliance of the system to be unfounded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 46 party` `Art 46 act`
`Art 46(5) the Commission's duties after an objection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 46(5) the duty of the paragraph applies` `the date asked` `the duty of the paragraph` `a Member State has raised objections within 15 calendar days against an authorisation issued by the market surveillance authority of another Member State` `the Commission considers the authorisation to be contrary to Union law, or the conclusion of the Member States regarding the compliance of the system to be unfounded`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `the duty of the paragraph`
        WHEN `Art 46(5) the Commission enters into consultations with the relevant Member State without delay` THEN PARTY `Art 46 the Commission` MUST `Art 46(5) enter into consultations with the relevant Member State`
        WHEN `Art 46(5) the operators concerned are consulted and have the possibility to present their views` THEN PARTY `Art 46 the Commission` MUST `Art 46(5) consult the operators concerned`
        WHEN `Art 46(5) the Commission decides whether the authorisation is justified` THEN PARTY `Art 46 the Commission` MUST `Art 46(5) decide whether the authorisation is justified`
        WHEN `Art 46(5) the Commission addresses its decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant operators` THEN PARTY `Art 46 the Commission` MUST `Art 46(5) address the decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant operators`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

@ref Art 46(6)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission considers the authorisation unjustified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 46 party` `Art 46 act`
`Art 46(6) the market surveillance authority's duty to withdraw the authorisation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 46(6) the authorisation must be withdrawn by the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned` `the date asked` `the Commission considers the authorisation unjustified`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN PARTY `Art 46 the market surveillance authority` MUST `Art 46(6) withdraw the authorisation`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts
